This product depends on the following third-party components, each under its
own permissive license (none is redistributed inside this package; pip
installs them from their own distributions):

- pypdfium2 (Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause) — wraps Google PDFium (BSD-3-Clause),
  used for PDF page rendering and text extraction.
- reportlab (BSD-3-Clause) — used to build PDF output.
- uharfbuzz (Apache-2.0) — HarfBuzz shaping so stacked Thai marks render
  correctly in generated PDFs.
- pdfplumber (MIT) — used for text-layer word bounding boxes.
- Pillow (MIT-CMU) — image drawing for redaction.
- PyThaiNLP (Apache-2.0) — Thai tokenization and NER library code.
- python-crfsuite (MIT) — CRF sequence labeling for the thainer NER engine.
- regex (Apache-2.0 AND CNRI-Python) — Unicode-aware pattern matching.
- httpx (BSD-3-Clause) — HTTP client for the optional LLM providers.

NER model (downloaded by PyThaiNLP on first use, not bundled in this package):

- Thai NER model `thai-ner-1-4.crfsuite` (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
  International, CC BY-4.0) — Copyright Wannaphong Phatthiyaphaibun.
  Source: https://github.com/wannaphong/thai-ner/
  License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Deployments that redistribute the model file must carry this attribution.

Bundled font (amphrang/engine/fonts/, used to draw Thai text into generated
PDFs — PDPA report, processing receipt, breach and DSAR artifacts):

- IBM Plex Sans Thai Looped (SIL Open Font License 1.1) — Copyright 2017 IBM
  Corp. with Reserved Font Name "Plex".
  Source: https://github.com/IBM/plex
  License text: amphrang/engine/fonts/OFL-1.1.txt (OFL-1.1 requires the
  license to travel with the font file; it ships inside the wheel).
  The TTF is the upstream face converted from WOFF2 to a container reportlab
  can read — container change only; the design, the name table and all 520
  glyphs are unmodified.

Optional components (installed separately via extras, not part of the core
distribution):

- fastapi / uvicorn / python-multipart (`amphrang[server]`) — local HTTP server.
- mcp (`amphrang[mcp]`) — Model Context Protocol server.
- torch / transformers / sentencepiece / sentence-transformers (`amphrang[ml]`)
  — optional WangchanBERTa NER engine and semantic Section-26 detector.
- paddleocr / paddlepaddle (`amphrang[ocr]`) — optional scanned-PDF OCR.

PyMuPDF (AGPL) is NOT used; it was replaced by the permissive libraries above
so this project can be distributed under the Apache-2.0 license.
